 "equipment_type": "Commercial boiler controller",
 "applies_to": "Hydrotherm (Mestek) KN and KN+ Series condensing boilers with a HeatNet V3 control board (firmware 4.20+), including HeatNet cascades of up to 16 boilers.",
 "summary": "The HeatNet V3 control on Hydrotherm KN and KN+ boilers exposes a fixed BACnet object list. The BMS writes heat demand, the system setpoint (guarded by a countdown failsafe timer), outdoor-reset settings, DHW setpoint, clock, and flow or boiler-count limits as analog and binary values. Read-only analog inputs give plant temperatures, boiler counts, BTU/h, system flow and per-boiler run time, cycles, temperatures, modulation and local flow; read-only binary values give interlock, alarm and status flags for each of up to 16 boilers.",
 "bacnet_transport": [],
 "firmware": "HeatNet control firmware 4.20+ (some points need 1.30, 2.00, 3.11 or 4.30)",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The object list does not say which BACnet data link (BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP) is used and gives no device instance or network settings.",
  "Per-boiler binary values are printed once as Boiler##_<name> with an instance formula and are listed here at the boiler 1 instance: 1000-series base + (n - 1) x 32, 2000/3000-series base + (n - 1) x 16. Boiler 1 is the master or stand-alone boiler; members are 2-16.",
  "Per-boiler analog inputs are printed as ranges and listed here for boiler 1 only: Runtime AI 48-63, Cycles AI 64-79, SupplyTemp AI 80-95, ReturnTemp AI 96-111, DHWTemp AI 112-127, Modulation AI 128-143, LocalFlow AI 152-167 (boiler n = boiler 1 instance + n - 1).",
  "Firmware: AV 16-17, AI 145 and BV 3012-3013 need 1.30+; AI 146-151 and BV 3014-3015 need 2.00+; AI 152-167 need 3.11+; AI 168-169 need 4.30+.",
  "No objects are printed at BV 1014, BV 1022 or BV 3004-3008. The document describes Boiler##_OutsideSensorNA with the same text as HeaderSensorNA ('Header Sensor not available'); the name suggests the outside sensor.",
  "Numbering largely matches Mestek's RBI HeatNet V3 list (RBI FIII/Fusion/CK) in this library; this Hydrotherm v2.00 list adds AI 152-169 and uses AI 7/8 for DHWTemp/StackTemp."
 ],
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Connect the BMS to the master (boiler 1) HeatNet control. Write BV 1 HeatDemand to call for heat and AV 2 Setpoint for the system setpoint, and keep reloading AV 1 SetpointTimer so the plant does not fall back to its local setpoint. Read header/supply/return temperatures, boilers on, modulation and the per-boiler alarm and failed flags.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 1",
    "name": "HeatDemand",
    "why": "Heat demand from the BMS (1 = heat)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 2",
    "name": "Setpoint",
    "why": "System setpoint, 40-220 °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 1",
    "name": "SetpointTimer",
    "why": "Failsafe countdown; reload before it reaches 0"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 144",
    "name": "OperatingSetpoint",
    "why": "Active setpoint in use"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 3",
    "name": "HeaderTemp",
    "why": "Header / system temperature, °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 1",
    "name": "BoilersOn",
    "why": "Number of boilers running"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 2",
    "name": "Modulation",
    "why": "System target modulation, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 1005",
    "name": "Boiler##_Running",
    "why": "Boiler 1 firing (add 32 per boiler number)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 1002",
    "name": "Boiler##_Alarm",
    "why": "Boiler 1 alarm (add 32 per boiler number)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 1003",
    "name": "Boiler##_Failed",
    "why": "Boiler 1 failed (add 32 per boiler number)"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BV 1 HeatDemand puts the boiler (plant) into heating mode when set to 1; 0 removes the demand. The setpoint the BMS writes is AV 2 Setpoint.",
  "heartbeat": "AV 1 SetpointTimer (0-65535 s) is a BMS failsafe countdown. The BMS must reload it periodically; if it reaches zero the control assumes the BMS has stopped and reloads its own saved local setpoint. Writing any read/write variable reloads the timer to 60 s if it is below 60 (on firmware below 3.48 only writing the setpoint does this).",
  "remote_sensors": "AV 16 BMSFlowRateGPM lets the BMS supply the system flow for flow-limited control, and AV 17 BMSLimitBoilers caps how many boilers HeatNet may run. AV 3-7 and BV 2 set up outdoor air reset; there is no writable outdoor temperature.",
  "setup": [
   "The object document gives no data link, address or device-instance settings.",
   "To set the clock, write AV 8-14 (month, day, year, hour, minute, second, weekday) and then write 1 to BV 3 SetClock."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "If SetpointTimer runs out, the plant quietly returns to its local setpoint.",
   "Per-boiler objects are listed at the boiler 1 instance; offset them by boiler number using the formulas in the notes. Boiler 1 is the master or stand-alone boiler.",
   "Per-boiler modulation (AI 128-143) does not work in AA/High Fire, T1 or T2 modes.",
   "BTUH (AI 146) is an estimate only.",
   "Several points need newer HeatNet firmware (1.30, 2.00, 3.11 or 4.30); see notes."
  ]
 },
